<h1>BEATZ: Product & Technical Implementation Plan</h1>
<div class="subtitle">1-Week Sprint MVP: Spotify Web Player & Queue Manager | Architecture & Division of Labor</div>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Sprint Target:</strong> Build a high-performance, focused web client that clones Spotify's real-time audio playback bar, queue drawer, and search-to-queue interaction using Next.js, Spotify Web Playback SDK, and Tailwind CSS.
</div>

<h2>1. Executive Summary & Partnership Roles</h2>
<p>To eliminate inter-team blocking and maximize velocity, this sprint adopts a <strong>Contract-First Architecture</strong>. We divide the workload strictly across domain boundaries:</p>

<div class="role-box">
  <div class="role-title"><span class="badge badge-be">Backend & API Architecture Lead</span> (Your Scope)</div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Authentication & Security:</strong> Spotify OAuth 2.0 PKCE flow, access & refresh token rotation, session management.</li>
    <li><strong>Audio Streaming Engine:</strong> Spotify Web Playback SDK script injection, device ID registration, and active playback transfer API.</li>
    <li><strong>REST API Wrappers:</strong> Resilient fetch endpoints for active queue (<code>GET /queue</code>, <code>POST /queue</code>) and track catalog search.</li>
    <li><strong>State & Hook Contracts:</strong> Zustand global state store and custom React hooks (<code>useSpotifyPlayer</code>, <code>useSpotifyQueue</code>) so frontend never touches raw API requests.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="role-box">
  <div class="role-title"><span class="badge badge-fe">Frontend & UI/UX Design Lead</span> (Partner Scope)</div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Design System:</strong> Modern dark Spotify theme (color tokens, typography, active status indicators).</li>
    <li><strong>Sticky Player Bar:</strong> Responsive bottom dock containing album art, track title, scrubber slider, transport buttons, and volume control.</li>
    <li><strong>Interactive Queue Drawer:</strong> Slide-over panel displaying currently playing song and upcoming queue list with reorder/remove UI.</li>
    <li><strong>Search & Track Cards:</strong> Clean search view with debounced input and one-click "Add to Queue" hover actions.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<h2>2. Day-by-Day Parallel Execution Matrix</h2>
<p>Both leads work concurrently each day without waiting on each other, using mocked interfaces on Days 1&ndash;3.</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 10%;">Day</th>
      <th style="width: 45%;">Backend & API Track (You)</th>
      <th style="width: 45%;">Frontend & UI Track (Partner)</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Day 1</strong></td>
      <td>Register app on Spotify Developer Dashboard; setup OAuth 2.0 PKCE flow; implement token storage and refresh logic.</td>
      <td>Scaffold Next.js + Tailwind project; define color tokens; create base application layout with header and content area.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Day 2</strong></td>
      <td>Build API client (<code>lib/spotify.ts</code>) with mock fallback responses; implement track search and queue endpoint wrappers.</td>
      <td>Build static <code>PlayerBar</code> UI using mock track data; design transport controls, scrubber slider, and album art layout.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Day 3</strong></td>
      <td>Inject Web Playback SDK script; implement <code>window.Spotify.Player</code> lifecycle listeners (ready, error, state_changed).</td>
      <td>Build static <code>QueueDrawer</code> slide-over component with mock song queue; implement open/close drawer transitions.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Day 4</strong></td>
      <td>Build Zustand global store (<code>usePlayerStore</code>); bind SDK events to store; build <code>transferPlaybackToDevice()</code>.</td>
      <td>Hook up <code>PlayerBar</code> to the Zustand store hooks (play/pause toggle, volume slider, seek bar, skip buttons).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Day 5</strong></td>
      <td>Connect real Spotify Queue API (<code>GET/POST /v1/me/player/queue</code>); implement optimistic state reordering.</td>
      <td>Connect <code>QueueDrawer</code> to real data; build debounced <code>SearchBar</code> with hover "Add to Queue" action.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Day 6</strong></td>
      <td>Handle edge cases: Non-Premium 403 error alerts, token expiry auto-refresh, and network drop recovery.</td>
      <td>Responsive design polish (mobile bottom sheet vs desktop dock), hover states, volume transitions, empty states.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Day 7</strong></td>
      <td>Integration verification (Auth &rarr; Stream &rarr; Queue &rarr; Search); environment variables check; Vercel deployment.</td>
      <td>Final design polish, typography consistency, presentation slides prep, live demo smoke testing.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>3. Shared Data Contract (TypeScript)</h2>
<p>This is the unified contract between backend data models and frontend components:</p>

<pre>
export interface SpotifyTrack {
  id: string;
  uri: string;
  name: string;
  durationMs: number;
  artists: { id: string; name: string }[];
  album: {
    id: string;
    name: string;
    images: { url: string; height: number; width: number }[];
  };
}

export interface PlayerPlaybackState {
  deviceId: string | null;
  isPlaying: boolean;
  currentTrack: SpotifyTrack | null;
  progressMs: number;
  durationMs: number;
  volume: number; // 0.0 to 1.0
}
</pre>

<h2>4. Critical Technical Constraints & Edge Cases</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Spotify Premium Requirement:</strong> The official Spotify Web Playback SDK requires an active <em>Spotify Premium</em> account to stream audio directly into the browser. Free accounts can authenticate and browse metadata, but audio streaming returns <code>403 Forbidden</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Browser Autoplay Security:</strong> Browsers (Chrome/Safari) block automatic audio playback until the user clicks on the page. The UI must trigger audio only after an explicit user interaction.</li>
  <li><strong>Token Expiration:</strong> Spotify OAuth access tokens expire after 1 hour (3600 seconds). The backend automatically handles refresh token rotation in the background.</li>
</ol>

